1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,408
In this town, there's one strange rule.

2
00:00:02,547 --> 00:00:04,910
Every house keeps one light on at midnight.

3
00:00:05,047 --> 00:00:06,144
No exceptions.

4
00:00:06,547 --> 00:00:08,373
My family moved here last week.

5
00:00:08,513 --> 00:00:10,280
Our neighbor warned us right away.

6
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,145
If your window goes dark at twelve...

7
00:00:12,247 --> 00:00:13,704
...the Night Mailman visits.

8
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:15,232
I thought it was a joke.

9
00:00:15,347 --> 00:00:17,594
My little brother Theo thought so too.

10
00:00:17,713 --> 00:00:19,602
He hated sleeping with the light on.

11
00:00:19,713 --> 00:00:21,461
11:59 PM.

12
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:22,719
He switched it off.

13
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:24,180
Then... silence.

14
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,136
Twelve o'clock. Something slid under the door.

15
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:31,202
Theo opened it.

16
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,313
It said: Your light is off.

17
00:00:33,413 --> 00:00:34,929
Come out and see ours.

18
00:00:35,047 --> 00:00:36,307
I ran to his room.

19
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:37,888
The window was open.

20
00:00:38,047 --> 00:00:41,113
I screamed. Mr. Pell was already at our door.

21
00:00:41,213 --> 00:00:42,439
Don't go out there.

22
00:00:42,713 --> 00:00:43,911
Light the lamp. Hurry.

23
00:00:44,213 --> 00:00:45,637
The room glowed gold.

24
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:47,642
Outside, the footsteps stopped.

25
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:49,319
By morning, he was home.

26
00:00:49,447 --> 00:00:50,951
But he just smiles now.

27
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:55,234
Every night at 11:59, he asks to turn off the lamp.

28
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,478
I never let him.

29
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,919
Keep your light on.

